SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillets: a contour stops at a vertex where the faces of both its edges
come tangent, each side's rounding vanishing there, and a walk into such
a vertex ends a hair before it, solved there step by step (mitcad#343).

The case: the bottom outline of a block over a post as wide as the block,
rounded with 1 after the post's foot was rounded with 10 (patch 0770):
along each long side the edge runs over the foot's rounding, whose face
comes tangent to the side at the point where the post touches it (the
foot's rounding ends in a point there, its surface degenerate at that
corner). OCCT carried the contour on through those points (the edges
continue each other there, FaceTangency, and the single case of
TangentOnVertex lets collinear edges go on); its walk crawled into the
point and stopped short of it, or its last section, the singular one given
at the point, took parameters on the degenerate face's iso far from the
contact's, and the approximation of the line between failed or wandered
(p-curve tolerances of tens of millimetres).

- TangentExtremity: where a face's surface has no normal at the vertex (a
  corner of a surface degenerate there), its normal is taken a little
  inside along the edge (its limit): the vertex is recognised as one where
  the faces come tangent.
- PerformElement: at a vertex where the faces of both edges come tangent
  the contour stops (downstream and upstream): each side is a stripe of
  its own, ending in a point at the vertex.
- ContactsAtTangentEnd: a walk towards such a vertex also ends where its
  section has no width any more (its contacts within Tol of each other)
  within a hundredth of the radius of the vertex.
- ChFi3d_EndBeforeVanishing (ComputeData, after the line is complete): at
  a tangency extremity the line's end is solved again from its last
  section at least 5e-4 of the radius wide, sections on towards the vertex
  each from the one before (its step on the faces no longer than the
  walk's step before, so no jump along a degenerate iso) until narrower
  than that within a hundredth of the radius of the vertex, where the line
  ends; the corner moves that end to the vertex (ChFi3d_ShrinkVanishingEnd,
  patch 0770), and the stripes there meet in the singular corner.

Upstream: new.
